1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Titles: Secretary to the Constable of Bourbon, an historian for Bourbon, Advocate General parliament of Paris, Auditor of accounts of Madame (Queen Mother) Louise de Savoy at Moulin.  Captain Lord of Montpensier.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the Family tomb, one can read this inscription "Hoc est sepulcrum familiae de Marillacis, quod oedificatum fuit, anno MDXVI" (This is the sepulchre of the de Marillac family constructed in 1516).
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert's epitaph  'Gilberti Marillaci a sancto genesio domini, a poissaco baroni incliti, multis nominum titulus clarissimi generosimic viri tumultus. (Translated as: 'The tomb of Gilbert  Marillac of the house of St Jean, and th
2 CONC e celebrated baron de Porsac illustrated by the number of titles, a generous man'.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert married Peronelle Filliol . They had a daughter Jeanne Peronelle who married Michel Of Veny, knight in armour, lord of Fernoel and Arbutus-Berry. He was also General of Finances and treasurer of France of Riom.   LA Vie p 
2 CONC 493
2 CONT
2 CONT La Vie p15 states that Aigueperse documents describe him in the following words: "Gilbert left not only a reputation as an eloquent and enlightened magistrate, and as a great Jurisconsult, but even that as a man of good. He freely
2 CONC  gave his advice to the poor and distributed his wages to plaintiffs who were not in circumstances to pursue their interests"
2 CONT
2 CONT Sgr de St Genest Baron of Porsac ( Alternative names: Puisac, Poisat, Porsa, Piosac) SECRETARY TO CHARLES DE BOURBON, CONSTABLE OF FRANCE OF WHOSE LIFE HE WROTE ABOUT
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert,  Baron of Porsac, Lord of S. Genest, Secretary of the Connetable of Bourbon.  Wife, Perronnelle Filliol.  They had one daughter.
