1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT From "The Mortimer Family of Wigmore: An outline lineage" by Ian Mortimer, Version 3.0, 16 June 2016 < [https://www.mortimer.co.uk/family/outlinelineage.pdf PDF] > Page 46-47
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean de Mortemer, seigneur of Couhé, who married first Philippe de la Rochfoucauld, dame de Roissac, and secondly Rosine de Pêrusse, by whom he had at least two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Guy de Mortimer (d. 1512), seigneur d’Ozillac et Roissac, who married Françoise Bouchard d’Aubeterre, dame d’Ozillac, by whom he had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  François de Mortemer (d. 1560), seigneur d’Ozillac et Roissac, who married Françoise d’Aydie de Ribérac, by who he had two daughters;
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. Jacquette de Mortemer, who married Louis de Rochfoucauld, seigneur of Montendre.
2 CONT *2. Anne de Mortemer, who married François de Reilhac, vicomte de Mérinvilleet de Brigeuil l’Ainé.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # "The Mortimer Family of Wigmore: An outline lineage" by Ian Mortimer, Version 3.0, 16 June 2016 < [https://www.mortimer.co.uk/family/outlinelineage.pdf PDF] > Page 46.
2 CONT # Watson, G.W. "Geoffrey de Mortemer and his Descendants", in Selby, Walford D. (ed. v. 1-5); Keith W. (ed. v. 6-10) Murray; and H.W. Forsyth (ed. v. 11-38) Harwood. The Genealogist (New Series). (London: George Bell & Sons) p. 1-
2 CONC 16. < [https://archive.org/details/genealogis_22selb/page/n32/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] >
