1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT http://www.fluckers.com/family/daspit/daspit1.html#Jacques Daspit de St.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre (Freire) Daspit  m. 1632 Madeliene de Cotten (or Cottes). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre Daspit4 , esquire, lord of the said manor and of Bavarlhes, magistrate and lieutenant at the siege of Frontigues, commissioner and deputy for the execution of the ordinances issued by the Duke d'Epernon, Kings governor of t
2 CONC he province of Guienne.  He is mentioned in an act of April 17, 16_7, containing an estimate for repairs to be made at the Castle of Castelviel, near Luchen.  By his marriage contracted in 1632, with the noble demoiselle Madeliene
2 CONC  de Cotten, he had three children, as follows: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard, who follows;  Joseph Daspit, esquire, lord of Lueviello, who had his coat of arms recorded in the General Armorial of France.  Jean Daspit, esquire, who was counsellor of the Court of Toulouse and Mayor of this city.  His
2 CONC  coat of arms is recorded in the General Armorial of France. 
