1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Was the head of King Henry III's (1551–1589) central administration and also served Henry IV (1553–1610) before dying in 1590 of a fever. His wife was forced to move the family to the home of her mother-in-law. As 
2 CONC Per: http://www.notablebiographies.com/Pu-Ro/Richelieu-Armand-Jean-du-Plessis-de.html
2 CONT
2 CONT >>_____________
2 CONT
2 CONT Professional soldier and courtier (later bishop) Jacques François du Plessis m Susanne de La Porte also of lesser nobility.
2 CONT  	As reward for the loyalty and service in serving Catholic King Henry III (1574-1589) against the Hugenots, the family was granted by royal approval the Bishopric of Luçon (department of Vendée) with Jacques François du Plessis n
2 CONC ow a Bishop as well as a soldier.  	 In 1590, when Armand Richelieu was just five years old, his father was killed during the continued French Wars of Religion. Armand's brother François du Plessis then became the next Bishop of L
2 CONC uçon (1590-1605). As Per: http://one-evil.org/people/people_17c_Richelieu.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>_____________
2 CONT
2 CONT =[http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haus_Le_Plessis-Richelieu   Jüngere Linie ]   [Younger Son of Guillaume III d 1373)'s Line]= 
2 CONT
