1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Carmelite nun at Pontoise at Marie du St Sacrement 
2 CONT
2 CONT Story La Vie p515
2 CONT
2 CONT La Vie p587
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptised in Paris on 6 Feb 1599.
2 CONT
2 CONT The only surviving daughter of Michel (Chateaudun).
2 CONT
2 CONT Despite an early attraction to the Ursulines, she decided to become a Carmelite and took the name Marie de St Sacrement.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the early death of her mother on 6 Feb 1600, she was made Pensionnaire (A boarder) of the Canonesses of St Augustine at St Etienne de Soissons.
2 CONT
2 CONT When she began to suffer from a violent Catarrh in her head and rheumatism in her neck, about the age of 4, her father brought her back home.
2 CONT
2 CONT She would have been only 2 months short of 8 when, on28 Dec 1607, Michel "gave" her (and his neice Innocente, the half sister of the later St Louise), to the newly founded Ursulenes.
2 CONT
2 CONT In her later deposition for the canonisation of Mme Acarie, (Beatified in June 1791 under the name Marie de la Incarnation) Valence stated that her father's friend often visited the Ursulenes offering counsel and assistance and "g
2 CONC iving order to the smallest things". For this reason, perhaps, she became attracted to the Carmelites which she entered in 1614.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon learning that the recently widowed Mme Acarie had just entered the Carmel house at Amiens, Valence followed her there 7 April 1614 and then went with her to Pointoise 2 years later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon reaching the canonical age, she took her vows on 12 Feb 1616. Her health was always threatened and she appeared more fragile than ever in 1618 during the final illness of her beloved mentor, Mme Acarie.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the last years of her life Valence never left the Convent's infirmary and it was to her that the Carmelites owe their particular sort of Hermitages.
2 CONT
2 CONT She fervently prayed for the conversion of Walter de Montaigu, an English secret agent in France, close to the Carmelites. He converted in 1635 and became a priest in 1654 and celebrated his first Mass at the Church the Pontiose C
2 CONC armels.
2 CONT
2 CONT She wrote a mystical treatise on some words of Job and from time to time received spiritual visions.
