2 CONT The bicone Castle was the seat of the family stronghold of Marillac from the late fifteenth century until 1649, when Jeanne de Marillac sells stronghold of bicone Antoine Bergier.
2 CONT  His son dying without issue, left his wife bicone who remarried 30 May 1667 with Claude-Antoine de Rochefort d'Ally. The fee will be resold to Annet Foucher, Treasurer General of France. Around 1765, the stronghold of bicone pass
2 CONC ed, by purchase, Pierre-Jacques-Mac-Gregor Drumonond captain Scottish regiment. His wife had always revolution. The castle is a beautiful manor with a few remnants of the Middle Ages (wall, tower, towers).
2 CONT
