1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Voir [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_II_de_Guise '''Wikipedia...''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * Henry II de Lorraine, 5th Duke of Guise (Paris, April 4, 1614 – June 2, 1664, Paris) was the second son of Charles, Duke of Guise and Henriette Catherine de Joyeuse.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of 15, he became archbishop of Rheims, but the death of his eldest brother Francis in 1639 placed him in the dukedom the following year. He opposed Richelieu, and conspired with the count of Soissons, fighting in the Ba
2 CONC ttle of La Marfée in 1641. For this, he was condemned to death, but fled to Flanders in 1641. His property was seized by the king in 1641, for crime of lese majeste. Reprieved, he returned in 1643 and his confiscated property was 
2 CONC returned to him. Hoping to make good his family's ancient pretensions to the Kingdom of Naples, he joined the revolt of Masaniello in 1647. The "Royal Republic of Naples" was declared, appealing to the protection of France and nom
2 CONC inally headed by Guise (entitled doge in imitation of Venice). However, the tactless Guise rapidly alienated the Neapolitans, and wielded little influence with Cardinal Mazarin. He was captured by the Spaniards in 1648 when the re
2 CONC public fell, and held by them until 1652. He made a second attack on Naples in 1654, but it ended in failure, in part due to the presence of an English fleet under Robert Blake.
2 CONT
2 CONT Afterwards, he settled in Paris, becoming Grand Chamberlain of France to Louis XIV and going deeply into debt because of his expenditures for horses and entertainments.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his nephew Louis Joseph, Duke of Joyeuse.
