1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k760763/f3.planchecontact.swf
2 CONT
2 CONT Baron D'attichy- Succession from the Doni Cousins 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 6 May 1637 Conseiller of the Parliament of Paris
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 April 1643 Maitre de Requets
2 CONT
2 CONT Conseiller d'etat ordinaire 1660 to 1682
2 CONT
2 CONT Conseiller d'Honneur in the Parliament of Paris. Michel, (son of Rene VII-2) Lord of Ollainville, Conseiller au Parlement in 1637.  Became Maitre des Requete on 16 April 1643, Councillor of State in 1660, then Councillor of Honor 
2 CONC of the Parliament of Paris.  He resigned from the office of State Counselor in 1682.  Died on 29 November 1684 and was buried at the Convent of the Carmelites at fauxbourg St. Jacques in Paris. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was Jeanne Potier, daughter of Nicolas Potier, Lord of Ocquerre, Councillor of State, and of Marie Barre.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean died on 1 July, 1681.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Michel and Jeanne had five children
