1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00010416&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Louis Antoine was born on 2 August 1682, the son of Louis I de Brancas, duc de Villars, and his first wife Marie de Brancas. He was duc de Villars-Brancas, pair de France, comte de Maubec, baron d'Oise, de l'Isle-Champte
2 CONC rcier, marquis d'Apilly, and comte de Lauraguais. He was also governor of the town of Aix, and chevalier des ordres du Roi. In 1702 he had an infantry regiment named after him, which he exchanged for the Orléans regiment in 1709, 
2 CONC having served as aide-de-camp to the duke of Burgundy in 1708. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 4 December 1709 at the château de Sceaux he married Marie-Angélique Fremyn de Moras, daughter of Guillaume Fremyn, comte de Moras, and Marie Angelique Cadeau, and the matron of honour to the dauphine. They had three children of
2 CONC  whom only Louis II would have progeny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 2 September 1716 Louis obtained letters of confirmation for registration of the peerage status of his duchy of Villars, and he took his seat in the parliament on 7 September. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis was made a chevalier des ordres du Roi (knight of the royal orders of Saint Michel and Saint Esprit) on 3 June 1724. He died in Paris on 19 February 1760
