1 NOTE {geni:about_me} source :
2 CONT
2 CONT ===============================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geocities.com/villeneuve_connections/deVilleneuve2.html
2 CONT
2 CONT visited on October 28, 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT XIII. Hercule de Villeneuve, lord of Esclapon, born and baptized
2 CONT
2 CONT September 29, 1649, at Valensole (1), on May 26, 1678 did one
2 CONT
2 CONT transaction with Pierre de Villeneuve, count of Tourrettes (p. 181), by
2 CONT
2 CONT giving him the ground of Esclapon on which it had been discussed. (chr.
2 CONT
2 CONT de Tr.). He was consulate of Valensole; tried in Aix, November 26, 1708
2 CONT
2 CONT (pr.) in favor of his son, Jean-Baptiste and died November 5, 1714, at
2 CONT
2 CONT Valensole (r.p.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife I. Marguerite Arnoux, married p.c. on November 27, 1681 (pr.),
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of Vincent Arnoux, of the village of Riez, lawyer in
2 CONT
2 CONT Parliament, and of Claire de Gaudemar. She died August 24, 1686 (1).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===============================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geocities.com/villeneuve_connections/deVilleneuve2.html
2 CONT
2 CONT consulté le 28 octobre 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT XIII. Hercule de Villeneuve, Seigneur d' Esclapon, né et baptisé
2 CONT
2 CONT le 29 Septembre 1649, à Valensole (1), le 26 Mai 1678 fit une transaction avec Pierre de Villeneuve, coomte deTourrettes (p. 181), par quelle il lui cédait les terres d' Esclapon au terme de la discussion. (chr.
2 CONT
2 CONT de Tr.). Il fut consul de Valensole; testa a  Aix, le 26 Novembre 1708
2 CONT
2 CONT (pr.) en faveur de son fils, Jean-Baptiste et mourut le 5 Novembre 1714, à
2 CONT
2 CONT Valensole (r.p.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Epouse I. Marguerite Arnoux, marriee p.c. le 27 Novembre 1681 (pr.),
2 CONT
2 CONT fille de Vincent Arnoux, du village de Riez, avocat au parlement, et de Claire de Gaudemar. Elle mourrut le 24 Aout 1686 (1).
